.* WRKOBJ: the objects a name and type select, with their options.
:PNLGRP.
:COPYR.(C) Quartz Systems 2026
:CLASS NAME=OPTCL BASETYPE=ACTION.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=NAMECL BASETYPE='CHAR 10'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=KINDCL BASETYPE='CHAR 8'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=TEXTCL BASETYPE='CHAR 50'.
:ECLASS.
:VAR NAME=OPT CLASS=OPTCL.
:VAR NAME=OBJ CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=OBJTYPE CLASS=KINDCL.
:VAR NAME=OBJLIB CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=OBJATR CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=OBJTEXT CLASS=TEXTCL.
:LISTDEF NAME=OBJS VARS='OPT OBJ OBJTYPE OBJLIB OBJATR OBJTEXT'.
:KEYL NAME=KEYS HELP=KEYSHLP.
:KEYI KEY=ENTER ACTION=ENTER.
:KEYI KEY=HELP ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F1 ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F3 ACTION=EXIT.F3=Exit
:KEYI KEY=F4 ACTION='RETURN 4'.F4=Prompt
:KEYI KEY=F5 ACTION='RETURN 5'.F5=Refresh
:KEYI KEY=F9 ACTION=RETRIEVE.F9=Retrieve
:KEYI KEY=F11 ACTION='RETURN 11'.F11=Display names and types
:KEYI KEY=F12 ACTION=CANCEL.F12=Cancel
:KEYI KEY=F16 ACTION='RETURN 16'.F16=Repeat position to
:KEYI KEY=F17 ACTION='RETURN 17'.F17=Position to
:KEYI KEY=PAGEUP ACTION=PAGEUP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEDOWN ACTION=PAGEDOWN.
:EKEYL.
:PANEL NAME=WRKOBJ KEYL=KEYS HELP=WRKOBJH ENTER='RETURN 0' TOPSEP=SPACE.Work with Objects
:TOPINST.Type options, press Enter.
:LIST DEPTH='*' LISTDEF=OBJS VIEWS=2 SCROLL=YES.
:LISTACT OPTION=2 ENTER='CMD EDTOBJAUT OBJ(&OBJLIB./&OBJ.) OBJTYPE(&OBJTYPE.)' HELP='WRKOBJ/OPTIONS'.2=Edit authority
:LISTACT OPTION=3 ENTER='CMD ?CRTDUPOBJ OBJ(&OBJ.) FROMLIB(&OBJLIB.) OBJTYPE(&OBJTYPE.)' HELP='WRKOBJ/OPTIONS'.3=Copy
:LISTACT OPTION=4 ENTER='RETURN 4' HELP='WRKOBJ/OPTIONS'.4=Delete
:LISTACT OPTION=5 ENTER='CMD DSPOBJAUT OBJ(&OBJLIB./&OBJ.) OBJTYPE(&OBJTYPE.)' HELP='WRKOBJ/OPTIONS'.5=Display authority
:LISTACT OPTION=7 ENTER='CMD ?RNMOBJ OBJ(&OBJLIB./&OBJ.) OBJTYPE(&OBJTYPE.)' HELP='WRKOBJ/OPTIONS'.7=Rename
:LISTACT OPTION=8 ENTER='CMD DSPOBJD OBJ(&OBJLIB./&OBJ.) OBJTYPE(&OBJTYPE.) DETAIL(*FULL)' HELP='WRKOBJ/OPTIONS'.8=Display description
:LISTACT OPTION=13 ENTER='CMD ?CHGOBJD OBJ(&OBJLIB./&OBJ.) OBJTYPE(&OBJTYPE.)' HELP='WRKOBJ/OPTIONS'.13=Change description
:LISTCOL VAR=OPT USAGE=INPUT HELP='WRKOBJ/OPT'.Opt
:LISTCOL VAR=OBJ USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/OBJ'.Object
:LISTCOL VAR=OBJTYPE USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/OBJTYPE'.Type
:LISTCOL VAR=OBJLIB USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/OBJLIB'.Library
:LISTCOL VAR=OBJATR USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/OBJATR'.Attribute
:LISTCOL VAR=OBJTEXT USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/OBJTEXT'.Text
:LISTVIEW COLS='OPT OBJ OBJTYPE OBJLIB OBJATR OBJTEXT'.
:LISTVIEW COLS='OPT OBJ OBJTYPE OBJLIB'.
:ELIST.
:CMDLINE SIZE=SHORT.Parameters for options 5, 7 and 13 or command
:EPANEL.
:HELP NAME=WRKOBJH.Work with Objects - Help
:P.The objects the name and type select, in library order. Type an
option next to an object and press Enter; a command typed on the
command line runs as typed.
:P.F17 positions the list at the first object whose name is the
command line's text or after it; F16 does it again.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=KEYSHLP.Function keys - Help
:P.F3 leaves the display, F12 goes back one display, F5 reads the
objects again, F11 shows the other columns.
:EHELP.
.* Item, key and option help.
:HELP NAME='WRKOBJ/OPT'.Option
:P.Type the number of an option next to an entry and press Enter. The
options the list allows are shown above it; F1 on one of them explains
it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/OBJ'.Object
:P.The object of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/OBJTYPE'.Type
:P.The type of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/OBJLIB'.Library
:P.The library of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/OBJATR'.Attribute
:P.The attribute of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/OBJTEXT'.Text
:P.The text of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKOBJ/OPTIONS'.Options
:P.Type an option number next to one or more entries and press Enter.
The option runs for each entry it is typed next to, in order.
:PARML.
:PT.2=Edit authority
:PD.Type 2 next to an entry and press Enter to edit authority it. The
Edit Object Authority (EDTOBJAUT) command runs for the entry.
:PT.3=Copy
:PD.Type 3 next to an entry and press Enter to copy it.
:PT.4=Delete
:PD.Type 4 next to an entry and press Enter to delete it.
:PT.5=Display authority
:PD.Type 5 next to an entry and press Enter to display authority it. The
Display Object Authority (DSPOBJAUT) command runs for the entry.
:PT.7=Rename
:PD.Type 7 next to an entry and press Enter to rename it. The Rename
Object (RNMOBJ) command is prompted for the entry.
:PT.8=Display description
:PD.Type 8 next to an entry and press Enter to display description it.
The Display Object Description (DSPOBJD) command runs for the entry.
:PT.13=Change description
:PD.Type 13 next to an entry and press Enter to change description it.
The Change Object Description (CHGOBJD) command is prompted for the
entry.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
